the Greek Defense Minister panos  kammenos is paying a short visit to a  refugee camp on the outskirts of Athens  the camp was opened on Tuesday just in  time to meet the EU deadline we are  obliged to do our best to have all the  Welcome Center here but also our best to  stop this flow the stream of migrants  has become a serious problem for Greece  Athens used to be a transit stop but now  many are stuck in the city because they  are no longer permitted to cross the  border in the north here in this small  container village those who are not  allowed to continue their journey are  stranded africans Pakistanis Iranians  and Palestinians the people here in this  Campbell literally going nowhere most of  them have the permission to stay in  Greece for six months then they become  illegal few of the migrants expected to  be stuck in Greece many were taken by  surprise at the border to Macedonia stop  thinking I had returned back to at them  and then I think for collective  information for staying here in Greece  when I collect all information for the  situation here I will get this side of  me and stay here  but if those asylum claims are rejected  it won't be easy to deport the migrants  this is very difficult for the city it's  also difficult to send them back because  many countries do not accept them  so here again we need European  solidarity and most of all because of  the situation of economic crisis they  cannot even find work in this in this  country and in this city so it's even  worse than in the past  seeking asylum in crisis stricken Greece  for many migrants the prospects of  success are dim some haven't given up  hope of continuing their journey I'm  just trying to move on even borders are  closed or open I don't I don't care  because my life is very much much more  important than a border ok and I'm  deciding caring for my life not for  borders within 15 minutes panos kammenos  has finished his inspection of the camp  if the route to the rest of the EU  remains closed these visits are likely  to become a regular fixture on his  schedule
 

